# Database Schema — Blockchain-Integrated Land Registry

> Relational schema (PostgreSQL, 3NF) for Digiverify with ASBA-style fund blocking, multi-signature workflow, court actions, and audit logging.

---

## Entity Relationship Overview

```mermaid
erDiagram
    users ||--o{ properties : "owns"
    users ||--o{ sale_transactions : "buyer"
    users ||--o{ sale_transactions : "seller"
    users ||--o{ court_freeze_orders : "issued_by"
    users ||--o{ court_reversals : "issued_by"
    users ||--o{ audit_logs : "actor"

    properties ||--o{ sale_transactions : "subject_of"
    properties ||--o{ court_freeze_orders : "frozen"
    properties ||--o{ property_documents : "has"

    sale_transactions ||--o{ fund_blocks : "secures"
    sale_transactions ||--o{ multi_sig_approvals : "approved_via"

    court_freeze_orders ||--o{ court_reversals : "reversed_by"
```

### Key Relationships

| Relationship | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `users` → `properties` | 1:N | A user (owner wallet) can own many properties |
| `users` → `sale_transactions` | 1:N | A user can be buyer or seller in many transactions |
| `properties` → `sale_transactions` | 1:N | A property can appear in multiple transactions over time |
| `sale_transactions` → `fund_blocks` | 1:N | Each sale can have multiple fund-block attempts |
| `sale_transactions` → `multi_sig_approvals` | 1:N | Each sale collects multiple signature approvals |
| `properties` → `court_freeze_orders` | 1:N | Courts can freeze a property multiple times |
| `court_freeze_orders` → `court_reversals` | 1:1 | A freeze order can be reversed once |
| `properties` → `property_documents` | 1:N | A property can have many IPFS-backed documents |

---

## Table Definitions

### 1. `users`

Stores all registered participants — buyers, sellers, government authorities, courts, and banks.

```sql
CREATE TABLE users (
    id              UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    wallet_address  VARCHAR(42) NOT NULL UNIQUE,       -- Ethereum-style 0x...
    name            VARCHAR(128) NOT NULL,
    email           VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    password_hash   VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    role            VARCHAR(20)  NOT NULL
                        CHECK (role IN ('buyer','seller','authority','court','bank')),
    kyc_verified    BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
    kyc_document_hash VARCHAR(128),                     -- IPFS hash of KYC docs
    face_verified   BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
    is_active       BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,
    created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);

-- Indexes
CREATE INDEX idx_users_wallet   ON users (wallet_address);
CREATE INDEX idx_users_role     ON users (role);
CREATE INDEX idx_users_email    ON users (email);
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> `password_hash` must be stored using bcrypt/argon2. Never store plaintext passwords. `wallet_address` should be validated at the application layer for checksum correctness.

---

### 2. `properties`

Central registry of all land parcels with IPFS document anchoring and geospatial data.

```sql
CREATE TABLE properties (
    id                  UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    property_code       VARCHAR(40)  NOT NULL UNIQUE,   -- Human-readable ID, e.g. MH-PNE-2025-00142
    survey_number       VARCHAR(60)  NOT NULL,
    survey_details      TEXT,
    geo_lat             DECIMAL(10,7),                  -- Latitude  (±90.0000000)
    geo_lng             DECIMAL(10,7),                  -- Longitude (±180.0000000)
    area_sqft           DECIMAL(12,2),
    address_line        VARCHAR(512),
    district            VARCHAR(128),
    state               VARCHAR(128),
    document_hash       VARCHAR(128),                   -- Primary IPFS CID of title deed
    owner_wallet        VARCHAR(42)  NOT NULL,
    encumbrance_status  BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE, -- TRUE = encumbered
    status              VARCHAR(20)  NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'
                            CHECK (status IN ('active','frozen','under_dispute')),
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),

    CONSTRAINT fk_property_owner
        FOREIGN KEY (owner_wallet) REFERENCES users (wallet_address)
);

-- Indexes
CREATE INDEX idx_props_owner       ON properties (owner_wallet);
CREATE INDEX idx_props_status      ON properties (status);
CREATE INDEX idx_props_code        ON properties (property_code);
CREATE INDEX idx_props_survey      ON properties (survey_number);
CREATE INDEX idx_props_district    ON properties (district);
```

---

### 3. `property_documents`

Stores multiple IPFS-pinned documents per property (mutation entries, encumbrance certificates, survey maps, etc.).

```sql
CREATE TABLE property_documents (
    id              UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    property_id     UUID NOT NULL,
    document_type   VARCHAR(60)  NOT NULL,          -- 'title_deed', 'survey_map', 'ec', etc.
    ipfs_hash       VARCHAR(128) NOT NULL,
    description     TEXT,
    uploaded_by     UUID NOT NULL,
    created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),

    CONSTRAINT fk_pd_property FOREIGN KEY (property_id) REFERENCES properties (id),
    CONSTRAINT fk_pd_uploader FOREIGN KEY (uploaded_by)  REFERENCES users (id)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_pd_property ON property_documents (property_id);
```

---

### 4. `sale_transactions`

Tracks the full lifecycle of a property sale, from initiation through multi-sig approval to completion.

```sql
CREATE TABLE sale_transactions (
    id                  UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    property_id         UUID NOT NULL,
    buyer_wallet        VARCHAR(42) NOT NULL,
    seller_wallet       VARCHAR(42) NOT NULL,
    sale_price          DECIMAL(18,2) NOT NULL,         -- Max ~10^16 currency units
    buyer_signed        BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
    seller_signed       BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
    authority_signed    BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
    funds_blocked       BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
    smart_contract_addr VARCHAR(42),                    -- On-chain contract address
    tx_hash             VARCHAR(66),                    -- Blockchain tx hash
    status              VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'initiated'
                            CHECK (status IN (
                                'initiated','payment_secured','approved',
                                'completed','cancelled','expired'
                            )),
    expiry_at           TIMESTAMPTZ,
    created_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),

    CONSTRAINT fk_st_property FOREIGN KEY (property_id)   REFERENCES properties (id),
    CONSTRAINT fk_st_buyer    FOREIGN KEY (buyer_wallet)   REFERENCES users (wallet_address),
    CONSTRAINT fk_st_seller   FOREIGN KEY (seller_wallet)  REFERENCES users (wallet_address)
);

-- Indexes
CREATE INDEX idx_st_property ON sale_transactions (property_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_st_buyer    ON sale_transactions (buyer_wallet);
CREATE INDEX idx_st_seller   ON sale_transactions (seller_wallet);
CREATE INDEX idx_st_status   ON sale_transactions (status);
CREATE INDEX idx_st_expiry   ON sale_transactions (expiry_at)
    WHERE status NOT IN ('completed','cancelled','expired');  -- Partial index
```

---

### 5. `multi_sig_approvals`

Records each individual signature event on a sale transaction (buyer, seller, authority).

```sql
CREATE TABLE multi_sig_approvals (
    id              UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    transaction_id  UUID NOT NULL,
    signer_wallet   VARCHAR(42) NOT NULL,
    signer_role     VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL
                        CHECK (signer_role IN ('buyer','seller','authority')),
    signature_hash  VARCHAR(132),                       -- ECDSA signature
    signed_at       TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),

    CONSTRAINT fk_msa_txn    FOREIGN KEY (transaction_id) REFERENCES sale_transactions (id),
    CONSTRAINT fk_msa_signer FOREIGN KEY (signer_wallet)  REFERENCES users (wallet_address),
    CONSTRAINT uq_msa_unique UNIQUE (transaction_id, signer_role)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_msa_txn ON multi_sig_approvals (transaction_id);
```

---

### 6. `fund_blocks` (ASBA-style)

Models the Application Supported by Blocked Amount pattern — funds are frozen in the buyer's bank account rather than transferred, until the sale is finalized.

```sql
CREATE TABLE fund_blocks (
    id                  UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    transaction_id      UUID NOT NULL,
    bank_reference_id   VARCHAR(64) UNIQUE,             -- Bank's unique lien ref
    buyer_wallet        VARCHAR(42) NOT NULL,
    block_amount        DECIMAL(18,2) NOT NULL,
    currency            VARCHAR(3) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'INR',
    blocked_at          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    unblocked_at        TIMESTAMPTZ,
    bank_confirmed      BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
    bank_confirm_ts     TIMESTAMPTZ,
    status              VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending'
                            CHECK (status IN ('pending','blocked','released','failed')),
    bank_user_id        UUID,                           -- Bank officer who confirmed

    CONSTRAINT fk_fb_txn   FOREIGN KEY (transaction_id) REFERENCES sale_transactions (id),
    CONSTRAINT fk_fb_buyer FOREIGN KEY (buyer_wallet)   REFERENCES users (wallet_address),
    CONSTRAINT fk_fb_bank  FOREIGN KEY (bank_user_id)   REFERENCES users (id)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_fb_txn    ON fund_blocks (transaction_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_fb_buyer  ON fund_blocks (buyer_wallet);
CREATE INDEX idx_fb_status ON fund_blocks (status);
```

---

### 7. `court_freeze_orders`

Encodes a court order that freezes a property, preventing any sale or transfer.

```sql
CREATE TABLE court_freeze_orders (
    id                  UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    property_id         UUID NOT NULL,
    court_user_id       UUID NOT NULL,                  -- Court official who issued
    court_order_hash    VARCHAR(128) NOT NULL,           -- IPFS hash of court order PDF
    case_number         VARCHAR(60),
    reason              TEXT,
    frozen_at           TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    is_active           BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,

    CONSTRAINT fk_cfo_property FOREIGN KEY (property_id)  REFERENCES properties (id),
    CONSTRAINT fk_cfo_court    FOREIGN KEY (court_user_id) REFERENCES users (id)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_cfo_property ON court_freeze_orders (property_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_cfo_active   ON court_freeze_orders (is_active) WHERE is_active = TRUE;
```

---

### 8. `court_reversals`

Records the reversal of a court freeze, including previous-owner reference for restitution.

```sql
CREATE TABLE court_reversals (
    id                  UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    freeze_order_id     UUID NOT NULL UNIQUE,           -- 1:1 with freeze order
    property_id         UUID NOT NULL,
    court_user_id       UUID NOT NULL,
    reversal_order_hash VARCHAR(128) NOT NULL,           -- IPFS hash of reversal order
    previous_owner_wallet VARCHAR(42),                   -- Owner before freeze
    reason              TEXT,
    reversed_at         TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),

    CONSTRAINT fk_cr_freeze   FOREIGN KEY (freeze_order_id) REFERENCES court_freeze_orders (id),
    CONSTRAINT fk_cr_property FOREIGN KEY (property_id)     REFERENCES properties (id),
    CONSTRAINT fk_cr_court    FOREIGN KEY (court_user_id)   REFERENCES users (id),
    CONSTRAINT fk_cr_prev     FOREIGN KEY (previous_owner_wallet) REFERENCES users (wallet_address)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_cr_freeze   ON court_reversals (freeze_order_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_cr_property ON court_reversals (property_id);
```

---

### 9. `audit_logs`

Immutable, append-only audit trail for every significant action in the system.

```sql
CREATE TABLE audit_logs (
    id              UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    action_type     VARCHAR(60) NOT NULL,               -- e.g. 'PROPERTY_CREATED', 'SALE_INITIATED'
    actor_wallet    VARCHAR(42),
    actor_user_id   UUID,
    ip_address      INET,                               -- PostgreSQL native IP type
    property_id     UUID,
    transaction_id  UUID,
    metadata        JSONB,                              -- Flexible extra data
    created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);

-- Indexes (optimised for common queries)
CREATE INDEX idx_al_actor      ON audit_logs (actor_wallet);
CREATE INDEX idx_al_property   ON audit_logs (property_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_al_txn        ON audit_logs (transaction_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_al_action     ON audit_logs (action_type);
CREATE INDEX idx_al_created    ON audit_logs (created_at DESC);
```

> [!TIP]
> For production at scale, partition `audit_logs` by `created_at` using PostgreSQL native range partitioning (monthly or quarterly) to keep query performance high as the table grows to billions of rows.

---

## Relationship Diagram (Text)

```
users
  │
  ├── 1:N ──► properties              (owner_wallet → wallet_address)
  ├── 1:N ──► sale_transactions        (buyer_wallet / seller_wallet → wallet_address)
  ├── 1:N ──► fund_blocks              (buyer_wallet → wallet_address)
  ├── 1:N ──► multi_sig_approvals      (signer_wallet → wallet_address)
  ├── 1:N ──► court_freeze_orders      (court_user_id → id)
  ├── 1:N ──► court_reversals          (court_user_id → id)
  └── 1:N ──► audit_logs              (actor_wallet / actor_user_id)

properties
  ├── 1:N ──► property_documents       (property_id → id)
  ├── 1:N ──► sale_transactions        (property_id → id)
  ├── 1:N ──► court_freeze_orders      (property_id → id)
  └── 1:N ──► court_reversals          (property_id → id)

sale_transactions
  ├── 1:N ──► fund_blocks              (transaction_id → id)
  └── 1:N ──► multi_sig_approvals      (transaction_id → id)

court_freeze_orders
  └── 1:1 ──► court_reversals          (freeze_order_id → id)
```

---

## Security Notes

| Concern | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| **Password storage** | Use bcrypt (cost ≥ 12) or argon2id. Never store plaintext. |
| **Wallet address validation** | Validate EIP-55 checksum at the application layer before INSERT. |
| **Row-level security** | Enable PostgreSQL RLS so users can only query their own rows (except `authority`/`court`). |
| **Audit log immutability** | Revoke `UPDATE` and `DELETE` on `audit_logs` for application roles. Grant only `INSERT` and `SELECT`. |
| **Encryption at rest** | Enable PostgreSQL TDE or use disk-level encryption (LUKS / BitLocker). |
| **Sensitive columns** | Encrypt `kyc_document_hash` and PII fields using `pgcrypto` `pgp_sym_encrypt`. |
| **Connection security** | Enforce `sslmode=verify-full` on all database connections. |
| **SQL injection** | Always use parameterised queries (`$1`, `$2`, ...) — already followed in the codebase. |

---

## Indexing & Scalability Notes

| Strategy | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Primary keys** | UUID v4 — avoids sequential guessing attacks and allows distributed ID generation. |
| **Partial indexes** | `idx_st_expiry` filters out completed transactions; `idx_cfo_active` filters inactive freezes — these dramatically reduce index size. |
| **Composite indexes** | Add [(property_id, status)](file:///c:/Users/Akshay/Desktop/Digiverify/backend/models/User.js#21-33) on `sale_transactions` if queries frequently filter by both. |
| **Table partitioning** | Partition `audit_logs` by month on `created_at`. Consider partitioning `sale_transactions` by year if volume justifies it. |
| **Connection pooling** | Use PgBouncer in transaction mode for high-concurrency workloads. |
| **Read replicas** | Route read-heavy queries (property search, audit log viewing) to streaming replicas. |
| **VACUUM tuning** | Set aggressive autovacuum on high-churn tables (`audit_logs`, `sale_transactions`). |
| **Full-text search** | For property address search at scale, add a GIN index on a `tsvector` column derived from `address_line`, `district`, `state`. |

---

## Data Type Rationale

| Column Pattern | Type | Why |
|---|---|---|
| IDs | `UUID` | Globally unique, no sequence contention, safe for distributed systems |
| Wallet addresses | `VARCHAR(42)` | Ethereum addresses are 42 characters (0x + 40 hex) |
| Prices / amounts | `DECIMAL(18,2)` | Exact arithmetic for financial data, avoids floating-point rounding |
| Geo-coordinates | `DECIMAL(10,7)` | Sub-meter precision (~1.1 cm) — sufficient for parcel boundaries |
| Timestamps | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | Timezone-aware — critical for a multi-region system |
| IP addresses | `INET` | Native PostgreSQL type with built-in validation and operators |
| Flexible metadata | `JSONB` | Schemaless extension point for audit log details without schema migration |
| IPFS hashes | `VARCHAR(128)` | CIDv1 base32 hashes can be up to ~62 chars; 128 provides headroom |
